quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  10,98,"Why was there not a single town which had believed (without seeing the torment) so that its belief would have benefitted it, except the people of Yunus (Jonah)? When they believed, We removed from them the punishment of disgrace in this worldly life and granted them provision for some time."
  10,99,"If your Lord had so pleased, all those who were (living) on the earth would have surely believed. Would you then force people until they become believers?"
  10,100,And it is not for a soul to believe except by Allah’s leave. And He lays disgrace on those who do not use (their) reason (to understand the truth).
  10,101,Say: ‘Observe what is in the heavens and the earth.’ But neither signs nor warnings are of any benefit to those who refuse to believe.
  10,102,Are they waiting for (anything else) but the same (punishment) of the days of those (deniers) who passed away before them? Say: ‘Then watch and wait; I am also watching and waiting along with you.’
  10,103,"Then We delivered Our messengers and those who believed (with them). Thus, it is incumbent upon Us to save the believers."
  10,104,"Say: ‘O people, if you are in doubt about my religion, then (know that) I do not worship those (idols) whom you worship apart from Allah. Rather, I worship only Allah, Who causes you to die. And I have been commanded to be among the believers,"
  10,105,and that you should dedicate yourself to the religion as a man of pure faith and that you should never be among the polytheists.’
  10,106,"And do not worship (anything) besides Allah, which can neither benefit you nor harm you—for if you do so, then you shall surely be among the wrongdoers."
